# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bitcoin_tax — NEVER commit personal/tax data or secrets.
# Real exchange exports live OUTSIDE this repo (e.g. ~/Documents/BitcoinTax/ReadOnly).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Encrypted vault and ANY decrypted/exported user data
*.pgp
*.gpg
*.asc
vault*
!/crates/btctax-store/src/vault.rs
*.vault
*-snapshot.*
snapshot.*
# Committed man pages are generated from the CLI command structure (no user/vault data);
# the `*-snapshot.*` rule above otherwise silently eats `btctax-export-snapshot.1`.
!docs/man/*.1
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Raw exchange exports / personal tax data (keep out of the repo entirely)
/data/
/samples/
*.xlsx
transaction_history*
trades-personal-*
transfers-personal-*
withdrawals-personal-*
*_Bitcoin_Activity_*
*.coinbase.*.csv

# Rust build
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Local tooling / settings (not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# CI/scripts: local PII-patterns file (never commit)
scripts/.pii-patterns
scripts/.pii-patterns.bak

# Generated man-page PDFs (build artifacts; gropdf embeds a timestamp → not reproducible).
# Regenerate with `make docs` / `cargo run -p xtask -- docs --pdf`. The .1 sources ARE committed.
docs/pdf/
# ★★ DERIVED, not enumerated (2026-09-13). Ten agent worktrees were given
#    CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<repo>/target-<agent>, and `make check` derived target-<agent>-clippy
#    beside each. None matched a rule here, `git add -A` swept them in, and GitHub REJECTED the
#    push: `index-pack failed` on 103.5 MB binaries over its 100 MB limit — 109 GB on disk,
#    ~205k paths in two commits, stripped by filter-branch before anything was published.
#    The first fix attempt hand-listed ten directory names and MISSED the five -clippy ones,
#    which is the same enumerate-instead-of-derive defect one level down. Hence a glob.
target-*/
target-clippy/
__pycache__/

# Offline oracle toolchain venv (taxcalc + the Python drivers) — build artifact, NEVER commit.
.venv/

# IRS primary-source PDFs — publicly available, fetched on demand, never committed.
# Each has a "<name>.pdf.txt" note beside it with its irs.gov URL and sha256.
#
# ★★ What the tests read is a COMMITTED DERIVED OBSERVATION of the PDF, and there are TWO of them,
#    because one document answers two different questions:
#      * design/forms/extract/<stem>.txt   — the TEXT LAYER (pdftotext), for every quotation and
#        line-set check. Held to its own PDF by `xtask forms extract --all --check`.
#      * design/forms/geometry/<stem>.json — the GEOMETRY: every word with its coordinates AND every
#        AcroForm box with its coordinates and its NAME. Held to its own PDF by
#        `xtask extract-geometry --all --check`.
#    Both checkers need the PDFs and are therefore commands a developer runs, never tests.
#
# ★★★ This comment used to say the text layer "IS what the tests read", full stop. That was FALSE for
#     six `xtask::form_delta` tests, which read AcroForm field SPELLINGS — something the text layer
#     does not carry — straight out of the PDF. They passed on the machine that had the PDFs and
#     could not pass on any fresh checkout, so CI's `test` job was red on ubuntu, macOS and Windows
#     for eight days (FR-165, fixed 2026-09-13: they read design/forms/geometry/ now). A stale
#     comment of exactly this shape misled an agent the same week (FR-160) — so if you add a third
#     derived artifact, add it here.
design/forms/**/*.pdf

# ★★ FR-172 — and the rule above is PATH-SCOPED, which is how a 187,143-byte IRS PDF came to be
#    committed at the REPO ROOT under the filename `--out` (a1c6fc849, 2026-09-05): a tool's `--out`
#    flag was consumed as a positional path, the file landed at the root where nothing guarded it,
#    and `git add -A` took it. It was found only because `tar -T` choked on the leading dashes.
#    Two guards, because the mechanism has two halves — a PDF where none belongs, and a FLAG that
#    became a filename:
/*.pdf
/-*

# Compiler ICE dumps — rustc writes these to CWD on an internal error. One was committed on
# 2026-08-02 and found by review r6 (N-1); it is build debris, never a source artifact.
rustc-ice-*.txt
# A reviewer agent's cargo target dir (worktree reviews build here, on disk, not in /tmp tmpfs).
target-review/
# `cargo doc` target dir used by review/sweep agents (on disk, not tmpfs).
target-doc/
